                <pb facs="0664" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.3 B 1/57</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">[No.] 1267</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 3351
                    of August 31 [<hi rendition="#italic">30</hi>], 1920,<anchor n="78"
                        xml:id="d291-f1"/> transmitting “for the information of the Department”, a
                    communication addressed to the President by the Secretary of the Permanent
                    Advisory Commission of the League of Nations on Military, Naval and Air
                    Questions, in which request is made that the Secretary General of the League be
                    furnished with information regarding the export of arms and munitions from the
                    United States “in accordance with the principles laid down in Article XXIII,
                    paragraph (d) of the Covenant, and in the Arms Traffic Convention”, signed at
                    Paris [and Saint Germain] on September 10, 1919.</p>
                <p>In reply to your despatch you are informed that it is not deemed practicable to
                    make an answer to the communication.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                            Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
